kvm-switcher for Debian and Raspberry Pi OS
================================================

This package installs the fixed Linux command and udev permission rules for
both hidraw and USB/libusb transports on the validated MSI 491CQPX. Only MSI
491CQPX is validated; other monitor models are experimental and untested.

The Debian maintainer is nexxyz <nexxyz@users.noreply.github.com>. The source
project and release asset location are:

  https://github.com/nexxyz/kvm-switcher

Install a local package with:

  sudo env DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive apt-get -y -o Dpkg::Options::=--force-confold install ./kvm-switcher_0.8.2-1_all.deb

Add the intended headless user to the device group, then log in again:

  sudo adduser USER kvmswitch

Unplug and replug the monitor USB path after the group change. The package
post-install action only ensures the `kvmswitch` group and does not reload or
trigger udev. After an install or upgrade, reboot or use the attended
`sudo udevadm control --reload-rules` command, then unplug and replug the
monitor USB path.

The shared configuration is:

  /etc/kvm-switcher/config.json

Examples:

  kvm-switch
  kvm-switch --profile Raspberry
  kvm-switch --input hdmi1 --kvm typec
  kvm-switch --input dp --kvm upstream

Bare `kvm-switch` changes the route using the one target marked
`"default": true`; it is not a probe. Legacy configs without a default remain
valid for named profiles, but need exactly one explicit true value for bare mode.

After the USB path has settled, run the delayed no-write diagnostic when needed:

  sleep 15; kvm-switch --probe-hardware 2>&1 | tee ~/kvm-switcher-probe.log

The probe enumerates exactly one fixed interface, opens and closes it, and
performs no report I/O.

The launcher sets KVM_SWITCHER_CONFIG to the package configuration only when
the caller has not already set that variable. Keep the monitor OSD available
for manual recovery and perform attended validation before relying on a new
unit or model.

Remove the package but keep configuration:

  sudo apt remove kvm-switcher

Purge the package and let dpkg remove its registered configuration file:

  sudo apt purge kvm-switcher

The package does not add arbitrary users or manually delete the kvmswitch group
or user configuration during removal. The release install helpers add only the
invoking account after a successful package installation.

The Debian package default under `/etc` is intentionally frozen. Portable and
exported example configs may evolve independently, but an existing system
config always wins during helper upgrades. A one-time upgrade from an older
package that installed a postrm may still run that old removal hook; keep
storage stable and disconnect the HDMI/monitor USB path during that transition.
Future package upgrades have no postrm action. The helper never applies an
exported config implicitly; use `sh ./install.sh --apply-config` deliberately.
